<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Roman–Parthian Wars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">54 BCE – 217 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-persian-wars">Roman–Persian Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Roman–Parthian Wars were the conflicts between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthian-empire">Parthian Empire</a> from 54 BCE to 217 CE, the first phase of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-persian-wars">Roman–Persian Wars</a>. They began with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-licinius-crassus">Crassus</a>'s disastrous defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-carrhae">Carrhae</a> in 53 BCE and centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>; the armies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trajan">Trajan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucius-verus">Lucius Verus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/septimius-severus">Septimius Severus</a> all sacked the Parthian capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ctesiphon">Ctesiphon</a>. The last war ended after the Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nisibis">Nisibis</a> in 217, shortly before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanians</a> overthrew the Parthians.</p></div>
